From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:59:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: recognise a Mesa host driver by its GL vendor

The buffer-storage capability is gated on inferring the host's map cache
type, and that inference tests the GL renderer string for "Mesa". Only
some Mesa drivers repeat the name there: Mesa's Apple Vulkan driver
reports renderer "zink Vulkan 1.4(Apple M1 Ultra (MESA_KOSMICKRISP))",
which the case-sensitive test does not match, so the host inferred no
cache type and withheld VIRGL_CAP_ARB_BUFFER_STORAGE.

Without that bit the guest driver cannot expose GL_ARB_buffer_storage,
and Mesa caps a guest that has everything else at OpenGL 4.3.

Every Mesa driver does name Mesa as the GL vendor, which is also what
the cache-type inference below already reads, so test the vendor string
first and keep the renderer-string tests for the drivers that answer
something else there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 682db3962fa509952a786b14b6deb4c02fa90bc5..74129d804475167b34cbd98f7da5aa772b38b99c 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -12755,7 +12755,10 @@ static void vrend_renderer_fill_caps_v2(int gl_ver, int gles_ver,  union virgl_c
 
    if (has_feature(feat_arb_buffer_storage) && !vrend_state.use_external_blob) {
       const char *vendor = (const char *)glGetString(GL_VENDOR);
-      bool is_mesa = ((strstr(renderer, "Mesa") != NULL) || (strstr(renderer, "DRM") != NULL) ||
+      /* A Mesa driver always names Mesa as the GL vendor; only some of them
+       * repeat it in the renderer string. */
+      bool is_mesa = ((vendor != NULL && strstr(vendor, "Mesa") != NULL) ||
+                      (strstr(renderer, "Mesa") != NULL) || (strstr(renderer, "DRM") != NULL) ||
                       (strstr(renderer, "llvmpipe") != NULL));
       /*
        * Intel GPUs (aside from Atom, which doesn't expose GL4.5) are cache-coherent.
